# Artha AI — Phase 3 Database Architecture

**Document type:** Architecture reference  
**Status:** Complete — Approved  
**Phases covered:** 3A through 3G  
**Depends on:** Phase 2 (AngelOne SmartAPI adapter)  
**Feeds into:** Phase 4 (Backtesting Engine), Phase 5 (Signal Engine)

---

## Executive Summary

Phase 3 designs the complete database architecture for Artha AI — a professional algorithmic trading copilot targeting Indian markets (NSE/BSE equities, NFO futures and options, MCX commodities). The architecture spans six functional modules: market data, trading pipeline, portfolio management, learning engine, operational infrastructure, and security/audit.

PostgreSQL with TimescaleDB is the chosen database engine. All design decisions are production-grade, optimised for Indian market trading workloads (50K ticks/s peak, IST timezone enforcement, NSE/NFO segment-specific cost and margin rules).

The Phase 3 architecture is fully approved and frozen. No modifications are permitted without a formal amendment document. Phase 4 (Backtesting Engine) and Phase 5 (Signal Engine) consume this schema as-built.

