## Database Architecture

### Technology choice: PostgreSQL + TimescaleDB

PostgreSQL was selected as the sole database engine. The rationale:

**ACID correctness** — real-money trading requires transactional integrity. A tick written half-way, an order committed without its execution leg, or a position balance that drifts are all catastrophic. PostgreSQL's full ACID guarantees are non-negotiable.

**Native JSONB** — semi-structured broker payloads (symbol master snapshots, strategy parameter blobs, feature vectors) stored without a separate document store. No impedance mismatch.

**TIMESTAMPTZ** — handles IST↔UTC conversion correctly at the storage layer. All timestamps stored UTC; all IST display logic lives in the application layer.

**TimescaleDB extension** — turns `ticks` and `candles` into proper time-series tables with automatic chunk management, continuous aggregates, and compression. No additional time-series database needed — one operational model throughout.

**Partial indexes** — hot-path queries on `status IN ('open','partial')` use tiny partial indexes, not full table scans.

**pg_partman + pg_cron** — partition management and scheduled jobs (compression, archival, metrics recomputation, instrument master sync) without external infrastructure.

**One database, one operational model.** No Redis, no MongoDB, no InfluxDB. Reduces operational complexity for a solo/small-team trading system.

### Six-module ownership model

Each module owns its data. No cross-module foreign keys except through the audit log. Module boundaries established in Phase 3A and honoured throughout 3B–3G.

| Module | Tables | Write volume |
|---|---|---|
| Market data | `symbols`, `ticks`, `candles`, `option_chain_snapshots`, `option_strikes` | Very high (ticks: ~50K rows/s peak) |
| Session state | `broker_sessions`, `active_subscriptions` (unlogged) | Medium (rebuilt on reconnect) |
| Trading pipeline | `signals`, `trades`, `orders`, `executions` | Low–medium |
| Portfolio | `accounts`, `portfolios`, `positions`, `equity_curve`, `performance_metrics` | Low–medium |
| Learning engine | `learning_records`, `strategy_performance`, `indicator_performance`, `regime_performance` | Low (batch, EOD) |
| Audit | `audit_log` | Mirrors all mutations |

### Tier model

**Hot layer** — `ticks`, `candles`, `broker_sessions`, `active_subscriptions`. High write volume, low latency reads required.

**Cold layer** — `trades`, `orders`, `executions`, `positions`, `learning_records`, `performance_metrics`. Relational, ACID-critical, lower write volume.

**TimescaleDB layer** — `ticks`, `candles`, `equity_curve` (1m grain). Time-series semantics, chunk-based compression and retention.

