## Architecture Review (Phase 3G)

### Strengths

The Phase 3 architecture is internally consistent across all six sub-phases. TimescaleDB hypertables on `ticks` and `candles` with chunk-local indexes, continuous aggregates, and compression are production-grade. The `symbols` central registry with `broker_token` as the SmartAPI bridge is correct and clean. The `signals → trades → orders → executions` chain in Phase 3C is correctly modelled with an append-only `executions` table preventing duplicate fills at the DB layer. The `mode` column on `trades` unifying live/paper/backtest into one table is the right call. The five-stage learning loop (trade close → learning record → pg_cron aggregation → signal engine reads → recalibrated weights) is architecturally sound. The three-tier index strategy (hot path partial / analytical covering / write path minimal) is appropriate for the trading workload.

